{#
  MY WORK — Figma 184:13749. The comp's three rows: ONTON, Challenquiz,
  Connect2WOW.

  THE ONE DARK BAND on the page, and the inversion lives entirely in the .work
  scope in tokens.css — this file and _work.css never name a colour.

  Renders the FEATURED projects that have card copy — `card`, not `status`, is
  what puts a project here. The two coincide today: all three rows have case
  studies. They have NOT always, and the filter is deliberately not "has a case
  study" — row 03 sat here while Connect2WOW's write-up was still unbuilt, and
  Ezam Part had a published page and no row until it was retired. The comp
  decides this section, and a project moves in or out by gaining or losing a
  `card`.

  The heading is the site's two-tone pattern — regular word, bold word — the
  same shape as the hero's "I'm Pari." and About's "About Me".
#}

{% from "components/project-card.njk" import projectCard %}

<section class="work" id="featured-works" data-header-theme="dark">
  <div class="work__inner">
    <h2 class="work__heading">
      <span class="work__heading-lead">{{ work.heading.lead }}</span>
      <span class="work__heading-rest">{{ work.heading.rest }}</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="work__rows">
      {%- for p in collections.workCards %}
        {{ projectCard(p, loop.index) }}
      {%- endfor %}
      {#- THE LAST ROW'S RUNWAY. It has to be a real element in the flow: a
          sticky box is constrained so its MARGIN box stays inside the container,
          so a trailing margin on the last row pushes the box and the boundary
          down together and buys it exactly nothing (measured: 0px of range).
          padding-bottom on .work__rows fails from the other side — padding is
          outside the content box the constraint reads. Only a sibling that takes
          real height moves the container's end past the last row. -#}
      <div class="work__runway" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
